:"?"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Whether this CA is offered as a trust anchor for mutual TLS. When set, the server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exports this CA’s ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"public","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" certificate to the bundle named by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AXIAM__SERVER__TLS__CLIENT_CA_BUNDLE_PATH"},{"text":" at startup and turns client-certificate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"authentication on (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optional"},{"text":") if the operator has not configured it explicitly. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"client presenting a certificate that chains to this CA is then verified by the TLS layer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"itself, which is what ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"axiam_pki::mtls"},{"type":"text","text":" needs to authenticate an IoT device or a service"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"account by certificate rather than by secret. # What is and is not copied Only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"public_cert_pem"},{"type":"text","text":" — the certificate. The "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"private key stays where its custodian put","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (Vault, or sealed into the row) and is never written to the server volume. A trust"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anchor is public by construction: it is what the server hands every client during the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"TLS handshake, and every device that has to validate the chain already holds a copy. #"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Why a restart rustls builds its "},{"code":"RootCertStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" once, when the listener is constructed,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and actix-web binds that config for the process’s life. Toggling this changes what the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"next","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" boot trusts, and the API says so in its response rather than pretending the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change took effect. Defaults to "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so a deployment that never touches this keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly the TLS posture it has today."}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cacertificate\/mtlstrustanchor","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CaCertificate\/mtlsTrustAnchor","role":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CaCertificate/keyAlgorithm":{"title":"keyAlgorithm","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"keyAlgorithm","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KeyAlgorithm","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK12KeyAlgorithmO"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The server’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"key_algorithm"},{"text":" field.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cacertificate\/keyalgorithm","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CaCertificate\/keyAlgorithm","role":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CaCertificate/chainPEM":{"title":"chainPEM","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"chainPEM","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The issuers above [","type"